!.env.example

# Agent sandboxes mask developer and editor configuration by bind-mounting an empty file over each
# path, so these appear in the worktree as zero-byte files that `git add -A` will happily stage.
# Listed without a trailing slash because the masked form is a file even where the real one is a
# directory, which is why the `.idea/` and `.vs/` patterns above did not match them.
# None of these is tracked. Should one ever need to be, `git add -f` says so out loud, which is the
# quieter failure of the two: the alternative leaves an empty file reappearing before every commit.
.bash_profile
.bashrc
.zshrc
.zprofile
.profile
.gitconfig
.gitmodules
.ripgreprc
.vscode
.idea
.mcp.json
.claude/agents
.claude/commands
.claude/hooks
.claude/output-styles
.claude/routines
.claude/workflows
.claude/launch.json
.claude/loop.md
.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
.claude/settings.json
